    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "I replaced `12544` literal with kernel arg, to make generated code simpler, and got the following ptx\r\n```\r\n\tld.param.u32 \t%r27, [kernel1_0d1d2d3d4d_param_4];\r\n\tshl.b32 \t%r28, %r26, 2;\r\n\tmov.u32 \t%r29, %ctaid.x;\r\n\tshl.b32 \t%r30, %r29, 10;\r\n\tor.b32  \t%r31, %r30, %r28;\r\n\tor.b32  \t%r32, %r31, 1;\r\n\tor.b32  \t%r33, %r31, 2;\r\n\tor.b32  \t%r34, %r31, 3;\r\n\tor.b32  \t%r35, %r31, 512;\r\n\tor.b32  \t%r36, %r31, 513;\r\n\tor.b32  \t%r37, %r31, 514;\r\n\tor.b32  \t%r38, %r31, 515;\r\n\tdiv.s32 \t%r39, %r31, %r27;\r\n\tdiv.s32 \t%r40, %r32, %r27;\r\n\tdiv.s32 \t%r41, %r33, %r27;\r\n\tdiv.s32 \t%r42, %r34, %r27;\r\n\tdiv.s32 \t%r43, %r35, %r27;\r\n\tdiv.s32 \t%r44, %r36, %r27;\r\n\tdiv.s32 \t%r45, %r37, %r27;\r\n\tdiv.s32 \t%r46, %r38, %r27;\r\n```\r\n`div.s32` is wrong, because dividend doesn't fit into s32, it can fit only in u32. ",
