    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "> int64_t indexing in cuda kernels is slower, but not dramatically so, ~15% penalty I'd say\r\n\r\nI think it can be much more than that. Since int64 registers take up 2 registers, this could cause register spilling and cause massive performance drop for e.g. matmul.\r\n\r\n> xnumel is correctly annotated as u32, but division result isn't, and I don't think it's expected even in C.\r\n\r\nYes, this part is a bug.\r\n\r\nThe way we've (temporarily) dealt with this problem at OpenAI has been to check on the host when the dimensions are too big, and to propagate this information via a constexpr, but this sucks so we definitely need a better way.",
